{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "The Natural World"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "A Story About a Shark "}, {"type": "position", "content": 9}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 12}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Identify and describe events in a range of social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn7le12ob09re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " The Passive Voice"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You often read or hear the passive voice being used in news reports. This is because the passive voice focuses the attention on the receiver of the action, rather than the doer of the action. In a news context, <span class=\"italic\">what</span> happened is more important than who acted. "}, {"type": "text", "content": " Here is an <span class=\"underline\">active sentence</span>:<br/><br/> (Subject + Verb + Object) <span class=\"italic\">A shark saved a father and son.</span><br/> <span class=\"italic\">\"The shark\"</span> is the focus of the sentence.<br/><br/>  Here is a <span class=\"underline\">passive sentence</span>:<br/> <br/> (Passive subject + To Be + Past Participle)  <span class=\"italic\">A father and son were saved (by a shark).</span><br/> <span class=\"italic\">\"The father and son\"</span> are the focus of the sentence."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Their lives were saved (by a shark)."}, {"type": "example", "content": "They were woken up (by a shark)."}, {"type": "text", "content": "It is often optional to include the agent, or doer, of the action in a passive sentence. This is because it is often unimportant or already understood within the context of the story."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " The Second Conditional - Talking About Hypothetical Situations"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you want to talk about an imaginary or hypothetical situation, you use the second conditional. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example: <br/> <span class=\"italic\">If I saw a shark, I would freak out!</span><br/><br/>  Are you going to see a shark? No.<br/> Is it possible to suddenly see a shark? Not really.<br/> What would happen if you saw a shark? You would freak out. <br/><br/> The second conditional contains both a condition clause (with if) and a result clause. "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"If\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Conditional\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Result\\\"}\",\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Simple Past\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"would + base verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> I went swimming,</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> I would check for sharks first.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> it suddenly started raining,</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> I would be stranded without an umbrella.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> I were you,</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> I would look into the different options for a cruise.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Remember to use a comma (,) after the IF clause. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "In conversation, it is common to use contractions. (<span class=\"italic\">I would</span> = <span class=\"italic\">I'd</span>)."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If I saw a shark again, I would remember this story and feel less hatred toward sharks."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I wouldn't go swimming if I knew there were sharks in the water."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "rubber raft"