": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn7le12ob09re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "text": "", "id": 0, "image": "engenn7le12ob09re2img01.jpg"}, {"time": "10", "text": "A father and son who were stuck on a raft in the ocean for four days without food or water said their lives were saved by a shark.", "id": 1, "image": "engenn7le12ob09re2img01.jpg"}, {"time": "7000", "text": "<p>Roy Thomas and his eight-year-old son, Jeremy, were alone in the ocean after their sailboat sank last Sunday. They had a tiny rubber raft to keep them afloat, but no food or water. After four days they were so weak that they could hardly move. Suddenly, they were woken by a shark.</p><p>\nThomas told how the shark swam up to the raft and tried to attack them. \"It was not the first shark we saw,\" Thomas told reporters, \"but this one really wanted to get us.\"</p>", "id": 2, "image": "engenn7le12ob09re2img03.jpg"}, {"time": "38000", "text": "<p>The shark was driven away by Thomas stabbing it on the back with a pocket knife. When his dad finished fighting off the shark, Jeremy saw a boat passing by. The father and son waved for help until the captain of the boat noticed them. The two were picked up and brought to safety.\"My Dad was a real hero,\" Jeremy said proudly, \"just like in the movies.\"</p> <p>\"Nevertheless,\" Thomas says, \"If I saw a shark again, I would remember this story and feel less hatred toward sharks.\u201d</p>", "id": 3, "image": "engenn7le12ob09re2img02.jpg"}], "coverimg": "engenn7le12ob09re2img01.jpg"}}], "template_override": 1, "type": "audio", "id": 1, "_data": [], "title": ""}]}]}